[SCENES STRUCTURE]
0.0–2.0s
Camera glides extremely close along the corroded hull of the colossal orbital colony, FPV proximity. Towers and cables pass by the lens.
Far below, a planet-scale electric superstorm rotates across the ocean. Lightning flashes illuminate the metal structure.

Sound: distant thunder, deep atmospheric rumble, faint electrical crackling.

2.0–4.0s
Blue plasma arcs crawl across antennas and communication towers as the charged atmosphere interacts with the station.
Sound: electric discharge crackling, low metallic vibration from the structure.

4.0–6.0s
The engines ignite violently.
Gigantic orange thrust columns fire downward toward the storm. Cloud layers distort under the sudden pressure.
Sound: massive rocket ignition, deep sub-bass impact followed by continuous engine thunder.
Music: slow industrial pulse begins.

6.0–8.0s
Camera dives beneath the station.
The exhaust column punches into the upper atmosphere.
Lightning attaches to the engine plume, climbing upward along the thrust column like electrical veins.
Sound: plasma discharge, electrical arcs snapping around the exhaust.

8.0–10.0s
Electrical discharges crawl across the hull. Ionized air glows faint blue along edges of towers and structural ribs.
The storm intensifies below.
Music: distorted low brass tones rising.

10.0–12.0s
First structural failure.
A fuel tank ruptures on one tower — violent industrial explosion.
Metal fragments spin away toward the storm.
Sound: compressed gas detonation, metal tearing.

12.0–14.0s
More failures cascade across the megastructure.
Antenna arrays shear off. Panels tear loose. Small plasma bursts flash along the hull while the engines continue burning.
Sound: sharp explosions, debris impacting metal.
Music intensity rising.

14.0–16.0s
A massive circular atmospheric shockwave ripple spreads across the storm clouds below. Lightning flashes across the expanding ring.
Sound: sudden pressure displacement boom followed by distant thunder.
Music: brief silence then deep bass impact.

16.0–18.0s
Directly beneath the engines, the eye of the storm collapses inward. Cloud walls distort and spiral violently under the thrust column.
Sound: roaring atmospheric turbulence.

18.0–21.0s
Camera pulls behind the station as it accelerates upward. Lightning continues attaching briefly to the exhaust plume before snapping away.
Debris streams backward through the charged air.
Music: heavy industrial rhythm.

21.0–23.0s
The colony punches upward into thinner atmosphere. Lightning fades behind it while engines continue burning.
Sound: storm noise fading, engines dominating.

23.0–25.0s
Earth rotates slowly beneath. The massive storm system churns far below.
The giant station climbs into black space.
Only the engine plumes remain glowing.
Sound: deep fading engine rumble.

Final frame
The colossal machine rises.


Music Direction

Sound design: 
Deep industrial cinematic score, dark ambient tension, heavy sub-bass pulses, metallic percussion, electrical storm textures, realistic rocket acoustics, no heroic melody.

Genre:
Industrial cinematic + dark ambient + low orchestral tension.

Tempo
~ 96–104 BPM
Slow but powerful.

Rhythm
Heavy pulse, not melodic.

Music Arc (25s)
0–4s — Atmospheric tension
Very low synth pad.
Sub-bass rumble slowly rising.
Storm electricity crackling.

No rhythm yet.

4–8s — Ignition moment
When engines fire:
deep metallic impact
Then a slow industrial pulse begins.
Boom … boom … boom.

8–14s — Escalation
Add:
distorted low brass
metallic percussion hits
deep synth drones
Music growing heavier.

14s — Shockwave moment
Music drops to near silence for 0.5 sec.
Then:
massive bass hit
This sells the atmospheric ripple visually.

14–20s — Chaos phase
Add:
distorted sub bass
industrial rhythmic hits
high electrical textures
Intensity peaks.

20–25s — Escape
Music simplifies again.
Only:
deep drone
slow pulse
faint choir pad
The machine survives.

